Agency Defendants for violating 40 U.S.C. § 8106, which mandates that a “building or structure

shall not be erected on any reservation, park, or public grounds of the Federal Government in the

District of Columbia without express authority of Congress.”

       If the Kennedy Center were slated to be demolished and rebuilt in some fashion, the

League might have a strong ultra vires claim on its hands, given the statute’s plain prohibition on

erecting buildings and structures without Congress’s express permission. Cf. Nat’l Trust, 2026

WL 877779, at *10–12 (holding that plaintiffs challenging East Wing ballroom construction

were likely to succeed on their Section 8106 claim because Congress had not authorized the

project). Any implication that Congress specifically approved the demolition and rebuilding of



