capacity as an ex officio Board member (with no legal right to vote), to challenge an action that

she agreed to in her capacity as a nonvoting member. Her claim of standing makes a mockery of

Article III, destroys the lawsuit’s basis, and reveals the nakedly partisan nature of her efforts.

       Even worse, Beatty’s claim further tarnishes this Court’s decision with Beatty’s appearance

