for relief; they did not themselves dissolve the injunction or decide the claims.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-24" data-record-href="/records/defendants-motion-vacate-88-2026-09-18/" data-passage="DEFENDANTS’ MOTION TO DISSOLVE PRELIMINARY INJUNCTION" aria-label="Source 24: read the evidence">24</a></sup><sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-25" data-record-href="/records/defendants-summary-judgment-89-2026-09-18/" data-passage="DEFENDANTS’ RENEWED MOTION FOR" aria-label="Source 25: read the evidence">25</a></sup></p><p data-layer="narrative">The supporting papers say the complete Delta report reached trustees on August 31 and that the board ratified closure on September 15. The defendants argued that phased closure would create a $300 million funding shortfall, compared with less than $30 million for full closure. These were the defendants' assertions. Floca's declaration identifies a JLL report and a Delta presentation as filed under seal.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-28" data-record-href="/records/defendants-statement-facts-89-2-2026-09-18/" data-passage="distributed the finalized Delta Consulting Group report, including its appendices, to trustees" aria-label="Source 28: read the evidence" data-passages="again voted over three dissents to ratify its earlier decision">28</a></sup><sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-27" data-record-href="/records/defendants-consolidated-memorandum-88-1-2026-09-18/" data-passage="a $300 million funding shortfall" aria-label="Source 27: read the evidence">27</a></sup><sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-29" data-record-href="/records/floca-declaration-89-3-2026-09-18/" data-passage="appears under seal on the docket" aria-label="Source 29: read the evidence">29</a></sup></p><p data-layer="narrative">Later on September 18, thousands joined the Hands Around the Kennedy Center protest, and some formed a human chain around the building.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-33" data-record-href="/records/ap-kennedy-center-protest-2026-09-18/" data-passage="Thousands of people joined outside" aria-label="Source 33: read the evidence" data-passages="formed a human chain around the center">33</a></sup></p></section><section id="unknowns"><p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">Open questions</p><h2 data-layer="fact">What we do not know yet</h2><ul data-layer="fact"><li data-absence>Whether the September 23 status report was filed, and whether the initial safety closure was extended. Searched: the admitted docket material and coverage through September 19; the report was not yet due.</li><li data-absence>Whether the defendants have developed a project-scope change that would trigger the notice order. The accessible public filings through September 19 do not identify an approved demolition plan. Floca's declaration identifies a JLL report and Delta presentation filed under seal; they were not available through the public storage route.</li><li>Trump's intent remained unresolved on September 18. The Associated Press reported that he did not directly respond when asked whether he planned to demolish the theater.<sup class="src-ref"><a href="#src-35" data-record-href="/records/ap-trump-kennedy-center-2026-09-18/" data-passage="did not directly respond when a reporter asked whether he planned to demolish the theater" aria-label="Source 35: read the evidence">35</a></sup></li><li data-absence>The court's minute order as a standalone, court-hosted document. Searched: the District Court docket, CourtListener and Justia; the docket routes were unavailable to the capture registry and the Justia mirror stopped before September 17. The page therefore labels the carriers of the quoted sentence.</li></ul></section><section id="records" data-layer="fact"><p class="sec-kicker">Sources</p><h2>The records</h2><p class="section-lede">Everything this page rests on, numbered where the story cites it. We keep a dated copy of each one.</p><h3 class="src-group">Primary documents</h3><ol class="src-list" start="1"><li id="src-1" value="1"><a href="/records/beatty-motion-84-2026-09-16/">Plaintiff motion for an emergency hearing</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-16 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; Beatty’s request for an emergency hearing over the closure</span></li><li id="src-2" value="2"><a href="/records/kennedy-bailey-declaration-84-1-2026-09-16/">Declaration of Bridget Kennedy-Bailey</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-16 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; firsthand observations submitted with the emergency motion</span></li><li id="src-3" value="3"><a href="/records/beatty-notice-85-2026-09-17/">Notice of supplemental authority</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-17 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the demolition placard and statements put before the court</span></li><li id="src-4" value="4"><a href="/records/defendants-response-86-2026-09-17/">Defendants’ response to the emergency-hearing motion</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-17 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the defendants’ account of the temporary closure</span></li><li id="src-5" value="5"><a href="/records/floca-declaration-86-1-2026-09-17/">Declaration of Charles Matthew Floca</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-17 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the sworn safety basis and initial duration of the closure</span></li><li id="src-6" value="6"><a href="/records/beatty-reply-87-2026-09-17/">Plaintiff’s reply in support of an emergency hearing</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-17 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; Beatty’s response to the temporary-closure account</span></li><li id="src-7" value="7"><a href="/records/preservation-joint-report-62-2026-08-28/">Joint meet-and-confer report</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-08-28 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the defendants’ no-demolition and no-new-structure position</span></li><li id="src-8" value="8"><a href="/records/preservation-addendum-62-1-2026-08-28/">Preservation plaintiffs’ addendum</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-08-28 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the preservation plaintiffs’ contemporaneous response</span></li><li id="src-9" value="9"><a href="/records/preservation-opinion-45-2026-05-29/">Memorandum opinion in D.C. Preservation League v. Trump</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-05-29 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the ruling that relied on the represented project scope</span></li><li id="src-10" value="10"><a href="/records/beatty-opinion-50-2026-05-29/">Memorandum opinion in Beatty v. Trump</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-05-29 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the legal baseline for closure and repairs</span></li><li id="src-11" value="11"><a href="/records/beatty-opinion-77-2026-09-15/">Memorandum opinion on the proposed recognition additions</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-15 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the September 15 ruling preceding the closure dispute</span></li><li id="src-12" value="12"><a href="/records/board-resolution-66-2-2026-08-13/">Kennedy Center board resolution on recognition additions</a> · Kennedy Center Board of Trustees, 2026-08-13 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the board’s separate recognition proposal</span></li><li id="src-13" value="13"><a href="/records/board-minutes-68-3-2026-08-13/">Kennedy Center board meeting minutes</a> · Kennedy Center Board of Trustees, 2026-08-13 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the main-building closure resolution and vote</span></li><li id="src-14" value="14"><a href="/records/board-vote-notice-78-2026-09-15/">Notice of the September 15 board vote</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-15 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the second board action before the emergency motion</span></li><li id="src-15" value="15"><a href="/records/scheduling-order-82-2026-09-16/">Scheduling order for expedited closure discovery</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-16 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the deadlines for the closure claim</span></li><li id="src-18" value="18"><a href="/records/beatty-counsel-reaction-2026-09-17/">Beatty counsel reaction to the notice order</a> · Washington Litigation Group, 2026-09-17 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; a party carrier for the minute order and the September 23 deadline</span></li><li id="src-24" value="24"><a href="/records/defendants-motion-vacate-88-2026-09-18/">Defendants’ motion to dissolve the preliminary injunction</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-18 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the request to dissolve the May injunction</span></li><li id="src-25" value="25"><a href="/records/defendants-summary-judgment-89-2026-09-18/">Defendants’ renewed motion for partial summary judgment</a> · U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, 2026-09-18 <span class="src-usage" data-layer="proof"> &middot; the renewed request for judgment on 
