generation for two years, if not far longer. See PI Mot., ECF No. 13-19 (“Borda Decl.”) ¶¶ 7–

15; ECF No. 13-20 (“Taylor Decl.”) ¶¶ 6–13; ECF No. 13-21 (“Borenstein Decl.”) ¶¶ 11–25;

ECF No. 13-22 (“Miller Decl.”) ¶¶ 11–17; see also Am. Amicus Br. at 8–13.

       In assessing Representative Beatty’s claims, then, the Court understands that the Center’s

trustees must discharge their relevant duties in a manner consistent with the common law of

trusts. And having cleared that brush, it is time to embark on an admittedly lengthy trek through

the many claims and issues raised by the competing motions before the Court. Let’s begin with

the Center’s renaming.



