pointed to no “public interest” that would be “disserved” by permanently enjoining the renaming.

And “[t]here is generally no public interest” in the “perpetuation” of “unlawful” governmental

action. League of Women Voters of the U.S. v. Newby, 838 F.3d 1, 12 (D.C. Cir. 2016).

