or the amici’s arguments.

         The Court lays out this evidence not to prescribe precisely what information the Board
should have considered. A board of trustees may act within the bounds of reasonable discretion
without necessarily following the same approach taken by similar institutions. But a failure to
consider any conceivable downside of such a weighty institutional decision reflects a dereliction
of the trustees’ duty of prudence.


